    "created_at": "2020-10-05T18:24:04Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-10-05T18:24:04Z",
    "body": "> * --status\r\n\r\ndoesn't exist in nushell - in powershell this would be `$LASTEXITCODE` and it's also a property when a property called like `p.ExitCode` when a `p = Start-Process` is called, bash it's `$?` i think.\r\n\r\n> * --cmd-duration\r\n\r\ndoesn't exist in nushell - if it's meant to time a command, we may be able to misuse `benchmark` for this\r\n\r\n> * --keymap\r\n\r\nwe have keymaps but I'm not sure what this parameter is meant to imply. If it's looking for a file perhaps, we could point it to a new keybindings.yml file somewhere?\r\n\r\n> * --jobs\r\n\r\ndoesn't exist in nushell\r\n\r\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
