    "body": "I'm also having this issue, but in bash.\r\n\r\nstarship version: 0.48.0\r\n\r\n`starship.toml`:\r\n\r\n```toml\r\n[character]\r\nformat = \"$symbol \"\r\nerror_symbol = \"[ERR](bold red)\"\r\nsuccess_symbol = \"[OK](bold green)\"\r\n```\r\n\r\n```\r\n/tmp\r\nOK starship --version\r\nstarship 0.48.0\r\n\r\n/tmp\r\nOK echo $BASH_VERSION\r\n5.0.17(1)-release\r\n\r\n/tmp\r\nOK false\r\n\r\n/tmp\r\nOK true\r\n\r\n/tmp\r\nOK echo $PROMPT_COMMAND\r\nstarship_precmd\r\n\r\n/tmp\r\nOK type starship_precmd\r\nstarship_precmd is a function\r\nstarship_precmd ()\r\n{\r\n    local NUM_JOBS;\r\n    STARSHIP_CMD_STATUS=$?;\r\n    NUM_JOBS=$(n=0; while read line; do [[ $line ]] && n=$((n+1));done <<< $(jobs -p) ; echo $n);\r\n    \"${starship_precmd_user_func-:}\";\r\n    eval \"$_PRESERVED_PROMPT_COMMAND\";\r\n    if [[ -n $STARSHIP_START_TIME ]]; then\r\n        STARSHIP_END_TIME=$(\"/home/k/.local/bin/starship\" time);\r\n        STARSHIP_DURATION=$((STARSHIP_END_TIME - STARSHIP_START_TIME));\r\n        PS1=\"$(\"/home/k/.local/bin/starship\" prompt --status=$STARSHIP_CMD_STATUS --jobs=\"$NUM_JOBS\" --cmd-duration=$STARSHIP_DURATION)\";\r\n        unset STARSHIP_START_TIME;\r\n    else\r\n        PS1=\"$(\"/home/k/.local/bin/starship\" prompt --status=$STARSHIP_CMD_STATUS --jobs=\"$NUM_JOBS\")\";\r\n    fi;\r\n    STARSHIP_PREEXEC_READY=true\r\n}\r\n\r\n/tmp\r\nOK cat 3; echo $?; echo $STARSHIP_CMD_STATUS\r\ncat: 3: No such file or directory\r\n1\r\n0\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis happens because `STARSHIP_CMD_STATUS` will **always** be zero, since it's set after `local NUM_JOBS`, which actually modifies `$?`:\r\n\r\n```\r\n/tmp\r\nOK f() { status_var_before=$?; local x; status_var_after=$?; }\r\n\r\n/tmp\r\nOK cat 3; f; echo \"before: ${status_var_before}, after: ${status_var_after}\"\r\ncat: 3: No such file or directory\r\nbefore: 1, after: 0\r\n```",
